.TH SAPHIRA-FIRSTBOOT-IMAGE 8 "October 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
saphira-firstboot-image \- dedicated installer wizard for the USB creator appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-firstboot-image
.SH DESCRIPTION
The USB creator appliance boots into this wizard instead of a login
prompt or the ordinary
.BR saphira-firstboot (8).
It guides the operator through choosing a destination disk, product,
firmware mode, filesystem, hostname, networking, DNS and root
password, shows the complete installation plan, requires an explicit
destructive confirmation, then installs onto the selected real disk
and offers a reboot.
.PP
The appliance is a temporary installation environment, never the
destination: every answer goes into the INSTALLED system only. The
wizard writes only the confirmed whole disk, never builds image
files, never modifies the created image afterwards except for the
documented network/DNS files, and never permits the appliance's own
boot disk as a target. Passwords live in memory only and are never
logged. Cancellation writes nothing at any point.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/saphira-image-firstboot-required
Setup owed marker, written at assembly. Spent on verified completion.
.TP
.I /var/lib/saphira-image-firstboot/
Session state (0600). Holds network staging, never passwords.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_IMAGE_TTY
Console device (default: /dev/console).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_IMAGE_MARKER
Marker path override (tests).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_IMAGE_DISK
Skip disk enumeration, use this device (tests).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_IMAGE_NOEXEC
Print the engine command instead of running it (tests).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_TMPDIR
Scratch root (never host /tmp).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-image (8),
.BR saphira-firstboot (8),
.BR saphira-install-plan (5)
